    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
      
      <!-- Topic 1 -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-500"></span>
          1. Dielectric Barrier Discharge & Interfacial RONS Generation
        </h4>
        <p>
          Cold atmospheric plasma (CAP) generated by dielectric barrier discharge (DBD) or high-frequency pulsed gliding arc in dry atmospheric air excites diatomic nitrogen (N₂) and oxygen (O₂) molecules without thermal heating. Electron collision dissociation generates ground-state and excited oxygen atoms (O(³P), O(¹D)) and nitric oxide radicals (•NO):
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-xl p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-ink space-y-1">
          <p>e⁻ + O₂ → e⁻ + 2 O(³P)</p>
          <p>O(³P) + O₂ + M → O₃ + M &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[Aqueous Ozone Precursor]</p>
          <p>e⁻ + N₂ → e⁻ + N(²D) + N(⁴S)</p>
          <p>N(²D) + O₂ → •NO + O &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[Nitric Oxide Radical]</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          When this energized gas stream is injected into water, secondary aqueous reactions yield short-lived hydroxyl radicals (•OH, E° = 2.80 V), superoxide anion (•O₂⁻), and long-lived reactive species including hydrogen peroxide (H₂O₂), nitrite ions (NO₂⁻), nitrate ions (NO₃⁻), and dissolved ozone.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Topic 2 -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-cyan-500"></span>
          2. Peroxynitrite Formation & Acid-Catalyzed Cytotoxicity
        </h4>
        <p>
          The primary driver of broad-spectrum bactericidal, virucidal, and sporicidal activity in cold plasma-activated water is peroxynitrous acid (ONOOH) and its conjugate base peroxynitrite (ONOO⁻). In acidified aqueous media (pH 2.8 to 3.8), nitrite ions react stoichiometrically with hydrogen peroxide:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-xl p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-ink space-y-1">
          <p>NO₂⁻ + H₂O₂ + H⁺ ⇌ ONOOH + H₂O &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[pKa = 6.8]</p>
          <p>ONOOH → [•OH + •NO₂] → NO₃⁻ + H⁺ &nbsp;&nbsp;[Rapid Cleavage, t_1/2 ~ 1.9s]</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          With a redox potential of E° = 2.05 V, ONOOH readily diffuses across neutral bacterial peptidoglycan walls and lipid bilayer membranes. Once inside, it initiates lipid peroxidation, oxidizes protein thiol groups (cysteine, methionine), and nitrates tyrosine residues in metabolic enzymes, inducing irreversible cellular collapse (>5.5-log kill) without selecting for antimicrobial resistance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Topic 3 -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-500"></span>
          3. Venturi Hydrodynamic Cavitation & Henry's Law Mass Transfer
        </h4>
        <p>
          Conventional gas bubbling columns suffer from low gas-liquid mass transfer efficiency (<18%) because large bubbles quickly escape into headspaces before RONS can dissolve. The continuous PAW reactor utilizes a precision sanitary AISI 316L venturi constriction:
        </p>
        <p>
          As pressurized water accelerates through the venturi throat, static pressure plunges below water vapor pressure (P_static &lt; P_vap), creating localized hydrodynamic cavitation. Plasma gas injected directly at this low-pressure throat is violently sheared by collapsing cavitation bubbles into micro- and nano-bubbles (mean diameter 20–50 µm). This increases interfacial surface area by >10,000-fold and achieves Henry's law dissolution efficiencies exceeding 92%.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Topic 4 -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-pink-500"></span>
          4. Clean-Label Nitrite-Free Meat Curing Kinetics
        </h4>
        <p>
          In clean-label meat manufacturing, consumers demand the elimination of synthetic sodium nitrite (E250) due to carcinogenic nitrosamine concerns, yet meat products require cured pink color, antioxidant stability, and Clostridium botulinum spore control:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline rounded-xl p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-ink space-y-1">
          <p>NO₂⁻ (aq) + H⁺ ⇌ HNO₂ ⇌ NO⁺ + OH⁻</p>
          <p>2 HNO₂ ⇌ NO + NO₂ + H₂O</p>
          <p>MbFe²⁺ (Myoglobin) + NO → MbFe²⁺-NO &nbsp;[Nitrosylmyoglobin (Pink Hue)]</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Under the acidic conditions of PAW (pH 3.5–4.2), aqueous nitrite ions naturally reduce to nitric oxide (•NO), which rapidly coordinates with the central Fe²⁺ heme iron of muscle myoglobin. Upon mild cooking (68°C–72°C), nitrosylmyoglobin denatures into nitrosohemochrome, delivering 100% equivalent color and shelf stability without synthetic preservatives or allergen-flagged celery powder.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sanitation & Curing Benchmarking Table -->
  <section class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">{d.tableTitle}</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Direct performance comparison between Continuous Hydrodynamic PAW and legacy industrial sanitizers and chemical curing salts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-hairline bg-surface-elevated text-ink font-bold">
            <th class="p-3">Sanitization / Curing Technology</th>
            <th class="p-3">Primary Active Mechanism</th>
            <th class="p-3">Pathogen Log Kill</th>
            <th class="p-3">Harmful Chemical Residues</th>
            <th class="p-3">Impact on Flavor / Color</th>
            <th class="p-3">Regulatory &amp; Clean-Label Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline text-body">
          {pawData.sanitationAndCuringBenchmarks.map((bench, idx) => (
            <tr class={idx === 0 ? "bg-purple-950/20 font-medium text-ink" : "hover:bg-surface-elevated/50 transition-colors"}>
              <td class="p-3 font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5">
                {idx === 0 && <span class="text-purple-400">★</span>}
                {bench.technology}
              </td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-[11px]">{bench.antimicrobialMechanism}</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-emerald-500">{bench.pathogenLogReduction}</td>
              <td class="p-3">{bench.chemicalResidues}</td>
              <td class="p-3">{bench.impactOnFoodFlavorColor}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-[11px]">{bench.regulatoryStatus}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<!-- Modeler Client-Side Simulation Script -->
<script>
  interface SubstrateData {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    category: string;
    recommendedOrpMv: number;
    recommendedPhRange: string;
    optimalNitritePpm: number;
    optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: number;
    optimalContactTimeSeconds: number;
    description: string;
  }

  const SUBSTRATE_MAP: Record<string, SubstrateData> = {
    organic_baby_spinach: {
      id: 'organic_baby_spinach',
      name: 'Organic Baby Spinach Leaves',
      category: 'Fresh Produce',
      recommendedOrpMv: 720,
      recommendedPhRange: '3.2 – 3.6',
      optimalNitritePpm: 35.0,
      optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: 115.0,
      optimalContactTimeSeconds: 60,
      description: 'Fragile organic leafy greens washed in continuous PAW. Achieves 5.3-log microbial kill while preserving cuticular wax, green chlorophyll pigmentation, and crisp turgor pressure without chlorine or chlorate residues.'
    },
    clean_label_frankfurter_meat_batter: {
      id: 'clean_label_frankfurter_meat_batter',
      name: 'Finely Emulsified Pork & Beef Frankfurter Meat Batter',
      category: 'Processed Meat / Clean-Label',
      recommendedOrpMv: 580,
      recommendedPhRange: '3.8 – 4.5',
      optimalNitritePpm: 160.0,
      optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: 65.0,
      optimalContactTimeSeconds: 120,
      description: 'Ground meat emulsion mixed with high-nitrite PAW (160 ppm NO2⁻). Acid-promoted nitric oxide binding to myoglobin forms stable nitrosylmyoglobin (MbFe²⁺-NO), yielding classic cured pink color and antioxidant stability without synthetic curing salts.'
    },
    shell_eggs_grade_a: {
      id: 'shell_eggs_grade_a',
      name: 'Commercial Grade A Whole Table Shell Eggs',
      category: 'Poultry & Egg Processing',
      recommendedOrpMv: 760,
      recommendedPhRange: '2.8 – 3.4',
      optimalNitritePpm: 45.0,
      optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: 140.0,
      optimalContactTimeSeconds: 30,
      description: 'Continuous high-speed spray sanitization of eggshells. Cold PAW penetrates microscopic pore fissures, neutralizing Salmonella biofilm within 30 seconds without thermal albumen denaturation or membrane damage.'
    },
    fresh_strawberries: {
      id: 'fresh_strawberries',
      name: 'Fresh Harvested Strawberries',
      category: 'Soft Fruit / Horticulture',
      recommendedOrpMv: 690,
      recommendedPhRange: '3.4 – 3.8',
      optimalNitritePpm: 25.0,
      optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: 95.0,
      optimalContactTimeSeconds: 45,
      description: 'Gentle immersion or misting of soft berries. PAW hydroxyl radicals and aqueous ozone destroy fungal conidia spores, doubling ambient post-harvest retail shelf life without fruit softening or calyx discoloration.'
    },
    broiler_poultry_carcass: {
      id: 'broiler_poultry_carcass',
      name: 'Eviscerated Broiler Chicken Carcass / Skin',
      category: 'Poultry Slaughter',
      recommendedOrpMv: 780,
      recommendedPhRange: '2.9 – 3.3',
      optimalNitritePpm: 55.0,
      optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: 165.0,
      optimalContactTimeSeconds: 40,
      description: 'Continuous pre-chill or post-chill immersion flume. High ORP PAW eradicates foodborne pathogens lodged in feather follicles and skin folds without chlorine bleaching or noxious organic acid off-odors.'
    },
    stainless_piping_cip_biofilm: {
      id: 'stainless_piping_cip_biofilm',
      name: 'AISI 316L Stainless Steel Dairy Pipework',
      category: 'Facility Sanitation & CIP',
      recommendedOrpMv: 820,
      recommendedPhRange: '2.5 – 3.0',
      optimalNitritePpm: 80.0,
      optimalPeroxynitriteMicromolar: 210.0,
      optimalContactTimeSeconds: 90,
      description: 'Clean-In-Place (CIP) recirculation through food processing equipment. PAW peroxynitrite and reactive radicals digest extracellular polymeric substances (EPS), destroying mature biofilms without chemical neutralization rinse cycles.'
    }
  };

  function initPawModeler() {
    const reactorSelect = document.getElementById('paw-reactor-select') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
    const substrateSelect = document.getElementById('paw-substrate-select') as HTMLSelectElement | null;

    const voltageSlider = document.getElementById('paw-voltage-slider') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const freqSlider = document.getElementById('paw-freq-slider') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const flowSlider = document.getElementById('paw-flow-slider') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const gasSlider = document.getElementById('paw-gas-slider') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const dwellSlider = document.getElementById('paw-dwell-slider') as HTMLInputElement | null;

    const voltageVal = document.getElementById('paw-voltage-val');
    const freqVal = document.getElementById('paw-freq-val');
    const flowVal = document.getElementById('paw-flow-val');
    const gasVal = document.getElementById('paw-gas-val');
    const dwellVal = document.getElementById('paw-dwell-val');

    const outOrp = document.getElementById('paw-out-orp');
    const outPh = document.getElementById('paw-out-ph');
    const outPeroxy = document.getElementById('paw-out-peroxy');
    const outNitrite = document.getElementById('paw-out-nitrite');
    const outLog = document.getElementById('paw-out-log');
    const outHue = document.getElementById('paw-out-hue');
    const outSei = document.getElementById('paw-out-sei');
    const outOzone = document.getElementById('paw-out-ozone');

    const statusPill = document.getElementById('paw-status-pill');
    const activeSubName = document.getElementById('paw-active-substrate-name');
    const activeDesc = document.getElementById('paw-active-desc');

    if (!voltageSlider || !freqSlider || !flowSlider || !gasSlider || !dwellSlider) return;

    function recalculate() {
      const vPeak = parseFloat(voltageSlider?.value || '15.0');
      const fAc = parseFloat(freqSlider?.value || '25.0');
      const qLiq = parseFloat(flowSlider?.value || '1200');
      const gasRatio = parseFloat(gasSlider?.value || '0.20');
      const tDwell = parseFloat(dwellSlider?.value || '45');
      const subKey = substrateSelect?.value || 'organic_baby_spinach';
      const subInfo = SUBSTRATE_MAP[subKey] || SUBSTRATE_MAP['organic_baby_spinach'];

      // Update text displays
      if (voltageVal) voltageVal.textContent = `${vPeak.toFixed(1)} kV`;
      if (freqVal) freqVal.textContent = `${fAc.toFixed(1)} kHz`;
      if (flowVal) flowVal.textContent = `${Math.round(qLiq).toLocaleString()} L/h`;
      if (gasVal) gasVal.textContent = `${gasRatio.toFixed(2)} L/L`;
      if (dwellVal) dwellVal.textContent = `${Math.round(tDwell)} s`;

      if (activeSubName) activeSubName.textContent = subInfo.name;
      if (activeDesc) activeDesc.textContent = subInfo.description;

      // 1. Electrical Discharge Power: P_elec (kW)
      // Empirical formula for DBD plasma: P = c * V^1.75 * f
      const pElecKw = 0.0035 * Math.pow(vPeak, 1.75) * (fAc / 20.0);

      // 2. Specific Energy Input (SEI in kJ/L)
      // SEI = (Power (kW) * 3600 s/h) / Flow (L/h)
      const seiKjPerLiter = (pElecKw * 3600) / qLiq;

      // 3. Reactive Species Yields (Nitrite, Peroxynitrite, Acidification)
      // Gas-to-liquid transfer scaled by venturi cavitation efficiency factor
      const massTransferEff = 0.88 + 0.10 * Math.min(1.0, gasRatio / 0.30);
      
      // Nitrite accumulation (mg/L or ppm)
      // High frequency and voltage increase NOx dissociation
      const rawNitrite = (seiKjPerLiter * 1.85 * (gasRatio / 0.20) * (fAc / 25.0)) * massTransferEff;
      const aqueousNitritePpm = Math.min(280, Math.max(8, rawNitrite));

      // Acidification (pH shift)
      // NOx dissolution forms HNO2 and HNO3
      const deltaHPlus = (seiKjPerLiter * 0.00012 * (gasRatio / 0.20));
      const simulatedPh = Math.max(2.2, Math.min(6.5, 7.0 - Math.log10(1 + deltaHPlus * 10000) * 1.85));

      // Peroxynitrite (ONOO- / ONOOH in µmol/L)
      // Formed from NO2- + H2O2 at low pH
      const rawPeroxy = (seiKjPerLiter * 3.2 * (gasRatio / 0.20) * ((7.0 - simulatedPh) / 3.0)) * massTransferEff;
      const peroxyYieldUmol = Math.min(320, Math.max(12, rawPeroxy));

      // 4. Oxidation-Reduction Potential (ORP in mV)
      // Baseline 220 mV, rises with peroxy and ozone and lower pH
      const orpMv = Math.min(880, Math.max(350, Math.round(220 + (7.0 - simulatedPh) * 58 + peroxyYieldUmol * 1.45 + (gasRatio * 180))));

      // 5. Pathogen Log Reduction (Log10 CFU/mL)
      // Chick-Watson model adjusted for ORP and dwell contact time
      const orpIntensity = Math.max(0.2, (orpMv - 400) / 320);
      const dwellFactor = Math.pow(tDwell / 45.0, 0.65);
      const logReduction = Math.min(7.5, Math.max(0.5, 3.8 * orpIntensity * dwellFactor));

      // 6. Nitrosylmyoglobin Cured Hue Index (%)
      // Requires NO2- in 80-200 ppm range and acidic pH < 4.8
      let curingHuePercent = 0;
      if (subKey === 'clean_label_frankfurter_meat_batter') {
        const nitriteAdequacy = Math.min(1.0, aqueousNitritePpm / 140);
        const acidityBonus = simulatedPh <= 4.2 ? 1.0 : Math.max(0.6, (5.0 - simulatedPh) / 0.8);
        curingHuePercent = Math.min(98.5, Math.max(40.0, 95.0 * nitriteAdequacy * acidityBonus));
      } else {
        curingHuePercent = Math.min(95.0, (aqueousNitritePpm / 150) * 85);
      }

      // 7. Catalytic Ozone Scrubber Exhaust Margin (ppm)
      // Unscrubbed ozone would be 12-45 ppm, with Carulite >99.98% destruction
      const unscrubbedOzonePpm = (pElecKw * gasRatio * 120) / (qLiq / 1000);
      const exhaustOzonePpm = Math.max(0.004, unscrubbedOzonePpm * (1 - 0.9998));

      // Update Telemetry Elements
      if (outOrp) outOrp.textContent = `+${orpMv} mV`;
      if (outPh) outPh.textContent = `${simulatedPh.toFixed(2)} pH`;
      if (outPeroxy) outPeroxy.textContent = `${Math.round(peroxyYieldUmol)} µM`;
      if (outNitrite) outNitrite.textContent = `${Math.round(aqueousNitritePpm)} mg/L`;
      if (outLog) outLog.textContent = `${logReduction.toFixed(2)}-log`;
      if (outHue) outHue.textContent = `${curingHuePercent.toFixed(1)}%`;
      if (outSei) outSei.textContent = `${seiKjPerLiter.toFixed(1)} kJ/L`;
      if (outOzone) {
        outOzone.textContent = `${exhaustOzonePpm.toFixed(3)} ppm`;
        if (exhaustOzonePpm > 0.08) {
          outOzone.className = "text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-mono text-red-500";
        } else {
          outOzone.className = "text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-mono text-emerald-500";
        }
      }

      // Status Pill Logic
      if (statusPill) {
        if (exhaustOzonePpm > 0.08 || simulatedPh < 2.5) {
          statusPill.textContent = "WARNING: EXTREME ACID / OZONE";
          statusPill.className = "px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-red-950 text-red-300 border border-red-800";
        } else if (subKey === 'clean_label_frankfurter_meat_batter' && curingHuePercent > 88) {
          statusPill.textContent = "OPTIMAL MEAT CURING";
          statusPill.className = "px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-pink-950 text-pink-300 border border-pink-800";
        } else if (logReduction >= 5.0) {
          statusPill.textContent = "HIGH-EFFICIENCY 5-LOG KILL";
          statusPill.className = "px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-emerald-950 text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-800";
        } else {
          statusPill.textContent = "NORMAL SANITATION DWELL";
          statusPill.className = "px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-purple-950 text-purple-300 border border-purple-800";
        }
      }
    }

    // Attach listener events
    [voltageSlider, freqSlider, flowSlider, gasSlider, dwellSlider].forEach(el => {
      el?.addEventListener('input', recalculate);
    });

    substrateSelect?.addEventListener('change', () => {
      const subKey = substrateSelect.value;
      const sub = SUBSTRATE_MAP[subKey];
      if (sub && dwellSlider) {
        dwellSlider.value = sub.optimalContactTimeSeconds.toString();
      }
      recalculate();
    });

    reactorSelect?.addEventListener('change', () => {
      recalculate();
    });

    // Preset buttons
    document.querySelectorAll('.paw-preset-btn').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const pType = btn.getAttribute('data-preset');
        if (pType === 'produce') {
          if (voltageSlider) voltageSlider.value = '14.0';
          if (freqSlider) freqSlider.value = '22.0';
          if (flowSlider) flowSlider.value = '1800';
          if (gasSlider) gasSlider.value = '0.18';
          if (dwellSlider) dwellSlider.value = '60';
          if (substrateSelect) substrateSelect.value = 'organic_baby_spinach';
        } else if (pType === 'curing') {
          if (voltageSlider) voltageSlider.value = '22.0';
          if (freqSlider) freqSlider.value = '36.0';
          if (flowSlider) flowSlider.value = '500';
          if (gasSlider) gasSlider.value = '0.35';
          if (dwellSlider) dwellSlider.value = '120';
          if (substrateSelect) substrateSelect.value = 'clean_label_frankfurter_meat_batter';
        } else if (pType === 'egg') {
          if (voltageSlider) voltageSlider.value = '15.0';
          if (freqSlider) freqSlider.value = '20.0';
          if (flowSlider) flowSlider.value = '1200';
          if (gasSlider) gasSlider.value = '0.22';
          if (dwellSlider) dwellSlider.value = '30';
          if (substrateSelect) substrateSelect.value = 'shell_eggs_grade_a';
        } else if (pType === 'cip') {
          if (voltageSlider) voltageSlider.value = '20.0';
          if (freqSlider) freqSlider.value = '30.0';
          if (flowSlider) flowSlider.value = '2400';
          if (gasSlider) gasSlider.value = '0.28';
          if (dwellSlider) dwellSlider.value = '90';
          if (substrateSelect) substrateSelect.value = 'stainless_piping_cip_biofilm';
        } else if (pType === 'hazard') {
          if (voltageSlider) voltageSlider.value = '24.5';
          if (freqSlider) freqSlider.value = '42.0';
          if (flowSlider) flowSlider.value = '150';
          if (gasSlider) gasSlider.value = '0.45';
          if (dwellSlider) dwellSlider.value = '180';
          if (substrateSelect) substrateSelect.value = 'fresh_strawberries';
        }
        recalculate();
      });
    });

    // Initial calculation
    recalculate();
  }

  // Initialize on DOM load and Astro page swap
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', initPawModeler);
  } else {
    initPawModeler();
  }
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initPawModeler);
</script>
